{#
  ChatComposer macro -- a chat input form with a text area that grows with its content, sends on Enter, and turns its send button into a stop button while a reply is in progress.

  A headless chat input form: a <textarea> and ONE button that is "send" normally and "stop" while `busy`.
  The send button is disabled, never hidden, when the value is empty or the form is disabled.
  MARKUP-ONLY DEVIATION: this catalog's macros ship no JavaScript, so the behaviours that need script — Enter to send (Shift+Enter for a line break, ignoring Enter during IME composition), growing the textarea as the user types, and swapping send/stop on the fly — are not in the macro. The macro renders the correct initial markup from its params (rows from the value's line count, send or stop from `busy`, the send button disabled when the value is empty); add a small client script (or use the Web Components catalog's element) for the live behaviour.

  HTML tag: <form>
  CSS class: chat-composer (sub-elements: chat-composer-input, chat-composer-button, chat-composer-button-label)

  Params:
    label        string   Required accessible name of the textarea (aria-label).
    sendLabel    string   Required word for the send button.
    stopLabel    string   Required word for the stop button.
    value        string   The text (the textarea's content).
    placeholder  string   Placeholder.
    name         string   Textarea name.
    minRows      number   Default 1.
    maxRows      number   Default 8.
    busy         boolean  A reply is in progress: the button becomes "stop".
    disabled     boolean  Disable the textarea and the button.
    id           string   Element id (on the form).
    classes      string   Consumer-provided extra CSS classes.
    attributes   object   Extra HTML attributes as key/value pairs (on the form).
    html         string   Raw HTML rendered before the textarea (attachments, model picker).

  Usage:
    {% from "components/chat-composer/macro.njk" import chatComposer %}
    {{ chatComposer({ label: "Message", sendLabel: "Send", stopLabel: "Stop" }) }}
#}
{%- macro chatComposer(params) -%}
{%- set p = params | default({}) -%}
{%- set lines = (p.value | default("")).split("\n") | length -%}
{%- set minRows = p.minRows | default(1) -%}
{%- set maxRows = p.maxRows | default(8) -%}
{%- set rows = lines -%}
{%- if rows < minRows %}{% set rows = minRows %}{% endif -%}
{%- if rows > maxRows %}{% set rows = maxRows %}{% endif -%}
<form
  class="chat-composer{% if p.classes %} {{ p.classes }}{% endif %}"
  {%- if p.id %} id="{{ p.id }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if p.attributes %}{% for k, v in p.attributes %} {{ k }}="{{ v }}"{% endfor %}{% endif %}
>
  {%- if p.html %}{{ p.html | safe }}{% endif %}
  <textarea
    class="chat-composer-input"
    aria-label="{{ p.label }}"
    rows="{{ rows }}"
    {%- if p.placeholder %} placeholder="{{ p.placeholder }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if p.name %} name="{{ p.name }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if p.disabled %} disabled{% endif %}
  >{{ p.value | default("") }}</textarea>
  <button
    class="chat-composer-button"
    type="{{ 'button' if p.busy else 'submit' }}"
    data-state="{{ 'stop' if p.busy else 'send' }}"
    {%- if p.disabled or (not p.busy and not (p.value | default("") | trim)) %} disabled{% endif %}
  ><span class="chat-composer-button-label">{{ p.stopLabel if p.busy else p.sendLabel }}</span></button>
</form>
{%- endmacro -%}
